WEBVTT

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:03.170
The Astrea Familia...

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.670
My most precious friends...

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.960
It's unlike you. Being so absent-minded, I mean.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.250
Is something the matter, Lion?

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.880
N-no, not really...

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:24.080
Goodness gracious. When did the noble and
sophisticated Elf turn into a lazybones, I wonder?

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.960
Asleep on her feet, no less...

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.880
Why, I could never hope to
achieve such a magnificent feat!

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.670
Kaguya! I assure you, I'm wide awake.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:37.670
And lose the snarky tone. It's extremely irritating.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.000
Oh, how frightening!

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:43.880
When did the Elf acquire
the poor etiquette of a Dwarf, I wonder?

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.790
C'mon, don't tease her like that, Kaguya.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:52.250
Isn't it obvious? She's distracted 'cause
she's fallen head over heels for a sexy dreamboat.

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.130
Wha-? Lyla!

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.080
Why must you make everything sound dirty?!

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:57.170
I would never-

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:59.540
Ah, so that's what it was, Lion!

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:03.710
How you met, how you fell in love...
Ya gotta give me ALL the details later, 'kay?

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.880
Please don't encourage her, Alise!

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.920
Well, I suppose it's time we get down to business.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:18.880
I've received intel from the Guild that Evilus
is up to something on the Lower Floors.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:22.330
Evilus... Do you mean the Rudra Familia?

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:23.500
Possibly.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:30.580
It's been a year since the Nightmare on the 27th Floor...
Evilus suffered a huge blow across the board.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.460
At this point, I’d imagine they can
only operate in the Lower Floors.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.750
They really got their asses handed to 'em, didn't they?

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:42.210
But I guess the Familias who allied with the Guild
didn't exactly walk away unscathed either...

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:48.330
Who knows what might have happened if the Loki
Familia hadn't been in charge of the counteroffensive...

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:49.000
Ah... a memory. Of that fateful day.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.830
That's what I'm sayin'.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.960
Just before disaster struck...

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:53.880
We owe it all to Braver, the pride and joy of us Prums!

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:55.710
And on that note...

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:00.080
We, the Astrea Familia, are going to conduct
an investigation on the Lower Floors.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.170
If we find something of interest, great.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:04.830
If we manage to foil the enemy's plan, even better.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:08.420
If we capture the Rudra Familia,
then that's cause for a celebration!

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:10.380
What an exciting idea.

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:11.080
No... No!

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:16.880
Should we happen upon them in the Dungeon,
I'll be sure to repay their heinous crimes in kind.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.420
The Rudra Familia, Jura...

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:15.880
they used that intel to lure us in!

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.460
I dunno... Seems like another trap to me.

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:23.130
Like that time on the 27th Floor.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:25.500
Maybe, but we gotta check it out.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:30.130
If it means preventing another tragedy
like that from happening, then we'll go!

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.250
Yeah, that's got "Alise" written all over it.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.130
Yep, you know me!

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.290
Okay, guys. Pack your stuff.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:39.130
Alrighty!

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.250
Roger!

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.920
Wait! You mustn't go down there!

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:47.040
Kaguya!

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.170
Lyla!

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:49.330
Neun!

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:50.580
Neese!

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:51.790
Asta!

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:53.080
Ryana!

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.290
Celty!

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:55.580
Isuka!

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:56.790
Marrue!

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:02.710
Alise...!

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:19.580
Is it Wrong to Try to Pick Up Girls in a Dungeon?  IV

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.830
Ignis

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.830
Flame

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:40.750
She's fast asleep.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.920
This might be the first time I've ever
seen Miss Ryu let her guard down...

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:48.210
Alise... Don't go...

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:50.290
She must be dreaming or something.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.500
A Skull Sheep...

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:01.630
Is its flock nearby? No, I only sense the one...

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:05.540
What do I do? If it's alone,
I should be able to take it down.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:09.630
But more of its friends might show up
when they hear the noise...

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:18.830
Come near me and I'll shoot. I will kill you!

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.540
It's different than the monsters on
the Upper and Middle Floors.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:25.290
They swoop in as soon as they spot their prey.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:28.130
Monsters on the Deep Floors are highly intelligent.

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:30.630
Which means there's a chance this might work!

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:35.790
It backed down...

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:41.540
Thank goodness. I can let Miss Ryu
rest for a little longer...

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:46.040
Oh, meow...!

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:50.500
What the heck happened?!

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:56.380
Has the Water Capital always looked like
a gaping hole leading straight to the pit of Hell...?

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:00.380
Nah, I've never seen it like this either...

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:05.210
If I had to guess, I'd say the Floor Boss
probably came charging through the cavern...

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:09.080
A Floor Boss from the Lower Floors
means Amphisbaena...

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:12.830
Is it pawssible someone fought it before we got here?

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:15.750
Okay, then where's the Floor Boss meow?

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.290
Y'think it bit the dust?

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:22.380
We don't know that for sure. The adventurers who
were fighting it might not have survived the battle.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:25.830
Precisely. There's only one thing we know for certain:

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:30.080
Unfortunately, whatever happened here,
we arrived too late to help.

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:33.500
Ryu oughtta be down on the 27th Floor!

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:35.130
Let's furget this place and go!

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:36.830
Easier said than done...

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.500
The whole Floor's falling apart!
The frickin' ground is missing!

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.710
What are we supposed to do?!

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:44.040
Hmm. Guess we've got no choice but to scale the cliff.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.080
Ugh, are you kitten me?

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:49.750
Don't worry! There aren't any
monsters around right meow!

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:52.040
So long as none show up, we'll be purrfectly fine!

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:57.380
My older brother used to go flyin' down these walls
by himself all the time! So we can do it, too!

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.540
H-hopefully...

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:05.380
Gods dammit!

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:07.210
Fine! Let's just scale the stupid thing!

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:09.790
It can't be cat bad...

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.250
Well, worst-case scenario,
we have to set a few broken bones.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:18.540
Cat's the spirit! Meow then...

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:19.710
Let's go!

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.750
BACK OFF!

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:25.170
Gimme a break!

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:27.420
No matter how many we kill, they just keep comin'!

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:32.290
Ouka, to your left!
And there's more closing in from behind!

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:33.670
They've got us surrounded...

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.130
There's way too many!

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:39.540
Don't bother trying to fight them!
We need to save our strength!

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:45.710
Their leader's wounded! Let's jump ship while we can!

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:52.750
This is the worst! It's been nonstop monsters
ever since we reached the 26th Floor!

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:56.670
At this rate, we won't have the time or
the energy to go looking for Rabbit Foot...

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.380
You're still hung up on that?

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:02.420
The plan to rescue Master Bell was set in stone
the moment we decided not to turn back!

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:06.080
Look, I get that you guys don't
wanna leave your friend behind.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.880
But how are we supposed to track him down
if we don't even know where to start?!

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.540
Moving forward is our only choice.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:16.380
We can't make our way back to the 24th Floor
until the Dungeon completes its repair cycle.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:21.830
So we've gotta find Bell Cranel and head
towards the safety point on the Lower Floors.

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:23.040
But-

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.500
That's where we're at.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:27.290
Any adventurer with a shred of
common sense would know to turn around

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:29.540
and follow the normal route back up.

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:31.750
Let's hope we run into him along the way.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:35.670
We still haven't escaped the despair...

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:37.420
But why...?

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:46.920
On your feet!

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:47.880
Something's coming!

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:53.750
A Kelpie?!

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:57.880
Kelpies spawn on the 27th Floor! How'd it get up here?!

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:03.830
RUN!

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.830
Lamias, Afancs, and Dodolas...

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:15.540
Are you kidding me?! Those are all 27th Floor monsters!

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:17.670
What in the world is going on?!

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:22.540
Ask the Dungeon! It's the one
who keeps jerkin' us around!

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:36.630
I swear, it's like the Dungeon's
got it out for us or something!

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:38.830
This is excessive, even for an Irregu-

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.080
Son of a bitch...

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:48.920
Ore from the Lower Floors...?

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:00.830
What's the matter with you, Ignis?!

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:01.880
Get up, now!

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.040
R-right!

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:09.330
A voice from farther down the tunnel!

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.710
It might be an adventurer on their way to the 27th Floor!

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:15.710
Ouka!

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:29.960
Hey, are you alright?!

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.880
Y-you're from Rivira...!

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:35.080
Master Bors?!

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:37.250
The Hestia Familia...!

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:41.130
Thank the gods, I'm... safe?

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:46.960
Are you alone?

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.630
What happened to all the others
who joined the manhunt?

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.380
They were murdered.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:56.750
Every last one of 'em, my men included...

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:57.460
What?!

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:01.250
That's impossible! Do you have any idea how
many high-class adventurers went with you?!

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:02.880
There were no survivors...?

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:04.880
You can't seriously expect us to believe that!

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:05.960
Simmer down.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:11.880
So you're tellin' me that Gale Wind managed
to turn the tables and wipe out your entire party?

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:14.830
No, not her. An Irregular.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:19.040
A new species of monster showed up,
one I ain't never seen before.

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:20.500
New species?

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:25.750
I'm sure you heard it, too.
That deafenin' roar when it spawned...

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:32.210
Now it makes sense. That was the sound of
the Dungeon setting some sort of monstrosity loose...

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.290
"The Great Disaster"...

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.500
That thing, it was unreal...

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:40.790
It can tear adventurers to pieces
with a single swipe of its claws...

00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:43.750
And there's no outrunnin' it, no matter how hard you try...

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.750
Um, Master Bors?

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:50.210
What happened to Master Bell?

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:55.170
Poor little Rabbit Foot didn't make it...

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:56.040
Wha-?!

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:01.670
Got one of his arms blown off,
and the way his neck snapped...

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:03.670
I doubt he survived...

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:05.710
You're lying.

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:07.170
I ain't lyin'!

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:10.830
Rabbit Foot, that stupid Gale Wind tryin' to protect me...

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.170
ALL of 'em! It was a bloodbath!

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.710
That monster massacred everyone!

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:17.630
THAT'S A LIE!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.630
Master Bell CAN'T die!

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:22.750
He's the one person in the world
who CAN'T abandon me!

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:24.080
Calm down, Lil Squeak!

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:30.170
But I... He can't...

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:32.830
There's no way he would do something like that!

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:34.330
Master Bell isn't...!

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:37.670
He can't be...

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:45.710
Please, no... Anyone but him...

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:56.290
Time to move!

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:57.630
Lil Squeak!

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:04.420
Master Bell is... dead?

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:06.130
If that's really true...

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.500
If Master Bell isn't alive anymore, then...

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:09.880
Monster incoming!

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:15.580
...then there's no point to any of this...

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.460
Oh crap! They're coming from the front, too!

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.130
It's gonna shatter the next time I use it...

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.380
And when that happens, we're screwed...

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:57.630
It's... a dead end.

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:04.540
If monsters attack us here,
there's quite literally no way out.

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:06.420
We need to hurry...

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:08.830
We need to get out of here as quickly as possible...

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:12.790
But... everyone's exhausted.

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:19.080
And besides, Master Bell is... gone...

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:25.580
Hey, Bors.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:26.250
What?

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:28.500
Tell me what you saw.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:30.960
Huh? But I already-

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:32.420
In more detail this time.

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:36.330
From beginning to end, specifically the part
about the creature attacking Bell Cranel.

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.630
None of that doom and gloom crap, either.

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:41.250
Describe exactly what went down.

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:47.710
Rabbit Foot, he... That thing ripped
his arm off with its claws.

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:54.460
And then... he took a pretty brutal blow to the neck...

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.210
His bones made a cracking noise.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:06.210
Look, I know a fatal injury when I see one...

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:11.210
Then what?

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:15.130
Are you telling me that you actually saw Bell Cranel's
corpse?

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:17.250
Huh? Well, no...

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:21.080
I saw Gale Wind casting some sorta healing magic...

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:24.130
But magic can't fix wounds like that...

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:26.880
Hold on a minute!

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:29.670
There's no way we can be absolutely certain he's dead!

00:15:30.170 --> 00:15:32.250
For all we know, he could still be alive, right?!

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:34.290
Er... Well, uh...

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:42.750
Given everything the kid's been through, he'd have
to be hangin' by a thread, but... I suppose it's possible...

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:47.250
It's Master Bell. Knowing him, I bet he's...

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:50.750
Yup. I got no doubt he managed to survive.

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:53.080
Our captain doesn't give up so easily.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:57.750
You heard the man! The plan hasn't changed.

00:15:58.210 --> 00:16:00.710
We keep heading towards
the safety point on the Lower Floors.

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:05.460
We might have one foot in the grave by the time
we get there, but we'll find Bell Cranel.

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:06.330
What?!

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:12.960
I JUST told you there's a freakish abomination roamin'
around the 27th Floor! I-I ain't goin' down there!

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:15.460
It'll be a cold day in Hell before I do that shit again-

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:22.630
I seem to remember something about
Gale Wind protecting you.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.630
I believe Bell Cranel's saved
your ass a couple of times, too.

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:30.580
For Bell Cranel or for Gale Wind.

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:34.250
If you've got ANY sense of gratitude,
then man the hell up.

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:39.790
A sliver of hope remains.

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:41.880
Perhaps for us as well...

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:46.830
So what you're saying is, we're about to embark
on a very long, very unforgiving journey.

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:47.790
Ugh, it figures...

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:53.080
She rallied the whole party...

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:56.420
That's the power of Antianeira, Lv. 4.

00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:01.080
Ordinarily, it would've been my job as the commander...

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.960
I need to work on getting stronger!

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:08.670
But if we're going to travel farther down,
we should head back to the normal route ASAP.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:11.790
There's basically only one way into this room.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:16.170
We have to leave soon, or else we're gonna get
pulverized by those monsters from the main area.

00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:18.790
You make a good point, but...

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:22.790
Let's take a short break first.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:26.040
Got it. I'll stand guard over by the exit.

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:28.500
Bors. Lend me a hand, wouldja?

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:29.290
Sure.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:32.250
Thank you, Lady Aisha and Master Bors.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:38.540
She may have gotten everyone on the same page, but
that doesn't necessarily mean our situation's improved...

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:45.080
Fend off and slip away from an onslaught of monsters.
That's the goal, but I can't come up with a solid strategy...

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.210
What do we do now?

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.330
How are we supposed to reach Bell?

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:51.290
Can we fight our way outta here?

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:55.000
If only I had another magic sword...

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:59.830
This thing's got one swing left before it breaks,
and it's not enough to keep the party safe...

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.420
"Stop weighing your pride against your friends, Welf."

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:05.880
I DID stop! It hasn't happened since!

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:10.210
And yet here we are, in danger and no magic sword.
So what's the frickin' point?!

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:11.830
Here, Master Welf.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.540
It's not much, but you should eat something.

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:17.960
Right... Thanks.

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:25.960
How can I help these guys out?

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:29.210
As a blacksmith, what can I do to give back?

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:31.880
Lady Hephaistos...

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:34.500
What's my best course of action here?

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:44.080
A hammer, some metal... And so long as you've got
a healthy flame, you can forge weapons anywhere.

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:52.330
Alright, everyone.

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:55.330
Are you willing to put your lives in my hands?

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:00.710
What do you mean?

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:04.080
I'm gonna rustle us up some magic swords.

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:04.920
Huh?

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:08.750
W-wait a minute! Rustle up magic swords...?

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.750
Build a makeshift workshop, to be more specific.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.250
Use it to craft new blades.

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:14.130
But that's-

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:16.920
As in, set up a forge to make swords HERE...?

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.750
HERE, where we could be
attacked at any given moment?!

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:20.460
Bingo.

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:22.130
How can you suggest something so absurd?!

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:26.540
This isn't even a safety point! Forging weapons
in the middle of a Floor that's crawling with danger?!

00:19:26.540 --> 00:19:28.540
Don't you need tools?! A hearth?!

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:31.080
What about the materials to actually make the swords?!

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:34.000
I brought a hammer and a hearth in case our gear
needed repairs.

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:40.290
I can light a fire with the blade we have.
And I picked up some materials a little while ago.

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:45.920
It's Adamantite. AKA the most
precious ore in the whole Dungeon.

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:48.130
Yes, but-

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:53.830
If we wanna wreck those ugly monsters and make it
to the 27th Floor in one piece, this is the only way.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.330
The magic swords... They'll get us there.

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:01.420
Once I start the forging process, I won't be able to move.

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:05.920
Which means that, until I'm finished crafting
the swords, you have to protect me.

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:08.670
So I need you to trust me with your lives!

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:12.000
Are you kiddin' me?! Have you lost your marbles?!

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:14.130
Who the hell would agree to a crazy plan like that?!

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:18.380
I don't care whether you think it's crazy!
You got a better idea?!

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:22.210
No? Then do you have faith in me or not?!

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:23.880
Answer me!

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:31.630
Let me ask you one question.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:35.170
Can you do it? Be honest.

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:40.880
You've got the hammer. You've got the metal.

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:45.580
So there's only one thing you need to ask yourself, Welf:

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:49.580
Your fire. Is it burning bright?

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.250
Of course I can!

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:57.210
So long as I've got a hammer, some metal,
and a healthy flame, I can forge weapons anywhere!

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:59.420
That's what us blacksmiths DO!

00:21:02.670 --> 00:21:04.460
Okay, then. Go for it.

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:06.460
Yeah. Forge away!

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:09.790
I have full confidence in you!

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:14.000
Oh, fine. If you must!

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:17.290
Yeah, I had a feeling this was gonna happen...

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:18.750
Daphne...

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:21.960
Gods-dammit! I ain't gonna stop ya...

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:27.920
Our lives... are in your hands.

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:30.130
Roger that!

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:32.750
I want everyone in their battle formations!

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:35.130
We're bettin' everything on Ignis!

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:44.250
No matter what happens, don't let any monsters get
close to Master Welf! Is that clear?!

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:04.290
Here goes nothin'.

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:40.040
Next Time

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:40.040
Welf Crozzo

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:40.040
Shikou

00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:38.630
Next time: "Welf Crozzo."
